comments:
@timheuer I was trying to design for the fact that some people might want to set the title to something other than the profile name. I don't really know _why_ you'd want that, but as @cinnamon-msft said:

>  the title of tabs will be configurable by the user, either with the path, shell name, name of their pet, etc. 

So someone could have the profile be named "Foo" and the tab text still say "Bar". Or even have the name be Powershell and the title text be `pwsh.exe`.

@DHowett-MSFT great work breaking that down, esp with screenshots.

Considering that case B.4 is useless, I'd lean towards implementing **A**.

At some point, we're going to need to just commit one way or another. In this case, there's pros and cons for both implementations, and I don't think there's a _clear_ winner. As long as the pros and cons are included in the spec doc, I'm fine just picking one, so long as we can come to a consensus.
